1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:02,026
Go back a few weeks.

2
00:00:02,026 --> 00:00:04,954
Chai Corner's second
outlet is only an idea.

3
00:00:05,254 --> 00:00:06,705
Ravi has no plan.

4
00:00:06,705 --> 00:00:07,928
Just one wish.

5
00:00:07,928 --> 00:00:08,870
Sell more.

6
00:00:09,420 --> 00:00:11,766
Without a plan, day one goes wrong.

7
00:00:11,766 --> 00:00:13,497
The milk runs out by ten.

8
00:00:13,797 --> 00:00:16,156
Nobody knows who should open the shop.

9
00:00:16,456 --> 00:00:18,995
And at night, nobody
knows if sales went up.

10
00:00:19,645 --> 00:00:21,448
A wish is not a plan.

11
00:00:21,448 --> 00:00:23,241
Ravi needs a real one.

12
00:00:23,941 --> 00:00:27,401
So Ravi sits down with his
team, weeks before opening.

13
00:00:27,751 --> 00:00:29,111
What will they do?

14
00:00:29,111 --> 00:00:31,028
Serve chai at a new outlet.

15
00:00:31,028 --> 00:00:31,928
How?

16
00:00:31,527 --> 00:00:32,828
With Asha's recipe.

17
00:00:33,178 --> 00:00:34,078
When?

18
00:00:33,713 --> 00:00:35,377
From seven every morning.

19
00:00:35,377 --> 00:00:36,277
And who?

20
00:00:36,113 --> 00:00:37,442
Meena will run it.

21
00:00:38,092 --> 00:00:39,197
That is planning.

22
00:00:39,497 --> 00:00:43,346
Planning means deciding in advance
what to do, how, when, and who will

23
00:00:43,346 --> 00:00:44,246
do it.

24
00:00:44,553 --> 00:00:46,830
Good planning follows seven steps.

25
00:00:46,830 --> 00:00:48,339
Watch Ravi use them.

26
00:00:48,689 --> 00:00:49,589
One.

27
00:00:49,189 --> 00:00:50,493
Set the objective.

28
00:00:50,493 --> 00:00:53,278
Two hundred cups a day at the new outlet.

29
00:00:53,628 --> 00:00:54,528
Two.

30
00:00:54,153 --> 00:00:55,255
Make premises.

31
00:00:55,255 --> 00:00:59,490
These are forecasts, like how
many people walk past each hour.

32
00:00:59,840 --> 00:01:00,740
Three.

33
00:01:00,399 --> 00:01:01,573
List the options.

34
00:01:01,573 --> 00:01:05,022
Near the college, at the
bus stand, or in the market.

35
00:01:05,372 --> 00:01:06,272
Four.

36
00:01:05,941 --> 00:01:06,979
Compare them.

37
00:01:06,979 --> 00:01:09,532
Rent, crowd, and rival tea stalls.

38
00:01:09,882 --> 00:01:10,782
Five.

39
00:01:10,480 --> 00:01:11,793
Choose the best.

40
00:01:11,793 --> 00:01:13,330
The bus stand wins.

41
00:01:13,680 --> 00:01:14,580
Six.

42
00:01:14,175 --> 00:01:15,661
Make supporting plans.

43
00:01:15,661 --> 00:01:18,205
Hire two helpers, and order the milk.

44
00:01:18,555 --> 00:01:19,455
Seven.

45
00:01:19,143 --> 00:01:20,625
Act, and follow up.

46
00:01:20,625 --> 00:01:23,290
Open, then check the numbers every week.

47
00:01:23,940 --> 00:01:26,187
Plans also come in three sizes.

48
00:01:26,187 --> 00:01:29,495
Strategic plans are the
big picture, for years.

49
00:01:29,495 --> 00:01:31,472
Five outlets in five years.

50
00:01:31,822 --> 00:01:34,784
Tactical plans turn that
into this year's steps.

51
00:01:34,784 --> 00:01:36,361
Open the second outlet.

52
00:01:36,711 --> 00:01:39,600
Operational plans are the daily details.

53
00:01:39,600 --> 00:01:41,294
Tomorrow's shift chart.

54
00:01:41,944 --> 00:01:44,249
But a goal like sell more is too vague.

55
00:01:44,599 --> 00:01:49,286
In 1981, George Doran wrote
that good goals should be SMART.

56
00:01:49,636 --> 00:01:52,122
Today, most people read it like this.

57
00:01:52,122 --> 00:01:53,022
Specific.

58
00:01:52,844 --> 00:01:54,941
Chai, at the bus stand outlet.

59
00:01:55,291 --> 00:01:56,191
Measurable.

60
00:01:56,093 --> 00:01:59,219
Two hundred cups a day,
so Kabir can count them.

61
00:01:59,569 --> 00:02:00,469
Achievable.

62
00:02:00,413 --> 00:02:04,092
Three hundred people pass
every hour, so it is possible.

63
00:02:04,442 --> 00:02:05,342
Relevant.

64
00:02:05,162 --> 00:02:07,512
It pays the rent of the new outlet.

65
00:02:07,862 --> 00:02:08,929
And time-bound.

66
00:02:08,929 --> 00:02:10,924
Within four weeks of opening.

67
00:02:11,274 --> 00:02:15,703
So sell more becomes, two hundred cups
a day at the bus stand, within four

68
00:02:15,703 --> 00:02:16,603
weeks.

69
00:02:16,911 --> 00:02:19,451
You can see this planning
at work every day.

70
00:02:19,801 --> 00:02:20,701
Objectives.

71
00:02:20,697 --> 00:02:24,886
A hospital sets a goal to cut
waiting time to twenty minutes.

72
00:02:25,236 --> 00:02:26,136
Premises.

73
00:02:26,019 --> 00:02:30,366
An ice cream maker expects a hot
summer, and makes extra stock.

74
00:02:30,716 --> 00:02:31,616
Options.

75
00:02:31,462 --> 00:02:35,625
A company compares three cities
before it opens a new office.

76
00:02:35,975 --> 00:02:36,875
Follow up.

77
00:02:36,819 --> 00:02:40,157
A sales team checks its
numbers every Monday morning.

78
00:02:40,807 --> 00:02:42,879
But can a plan see the future?

79
00:02:42,879 --> 00:02:43,779
Not fully.

80
00:02:44,059 --> 00:02:45,092
The good side.

81
00:02:45,092 --> 00:02:49,589
Planning gives direction, cuts waste,
and sets a standard to check against.

82
00:02:49,939 --> 00:02:51,016
The hard side.

83
00:02:51,016 --> 00:02:54,943
It takes time, and a fixed plan
can break when things change.

84
00:02:55,293 --> 00:03:00,568
In 1957, President Eisenhower
repeated an old army saying.

85
00:03:00,918 --> 00:03:03,566
Plans are worthless, but
planning is everything.

86
00:03:03,916 --> 00:03:04,952
So the lesson.

87
00:03:04,952 --> 00:03:08,015
Plan carefully, then be
ready to change the plan.

88
00:03:08,665 --> 00:03:09,595
Quick check.

89
00:03:09,595 --> 00:03:12,566
Asha's goal is to make
two hundred cups a day.

90
00:03:12,566 --> 00:03:14,531
Which SMART letter is missing?

91
00:03:16,431 --> 00:03:17,331
Time-bound!

92
00:03:17,302 --> 00:03:18,850
It has no deadline.

93
00:03:18,850 --> 00:03:20,839
Add one, like by Friday.

94
00:03:21,439 --> 00:03:22,452
So, remember.

95
00:03:22,752 --> 00:03:26,342
Planning means deciding in
advance what, how, when, and who.

96
00:03:26,692 --> 00:03:30,587
Follow the steps, from the objective
all the way to the follow up.

97
00:03:30,937 --> 00:03:32,514
And make every goal SMART.

98
00:03:33,114 --> 00:03:37,236
Next time, Ravi organizes his
growing team into departments.
